{{also|copout|cop-out}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Probably from [[cop a plea]]

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[cop]] [[out]]|cops out|copping out|copped out}}

# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} To [[avoid]] or [[shirk]], either by failing to perform, or by performing in a grossly [[insufficient]], [[negligent]], or [[superficial]] manner.
#: ''Faced with the prospect of cooking for himself, his first thought was to '''cop out''' and order a pizza.''
# [[plead]] [[guilty]] and ask for [[mercy]]

